==============================================================================
P5  the backward E-game in logarithmic charts (translation law = kappa formula)
==============================================================================
  departure chart delta(x) = log(2^eps x)/log 4 (eps = 0 if x=1 mod 3, 1 if x=2 mod 3),
  arrival chart i(y) = log(3y+1)/log 4.  Claim: a legal move k = 2n+eps(x) lands at
  y = (2^k x - 1)/3 with i(y) = n + delta(x), and v_3(y - h) = v_3(i(y) - i(h)) for every h.
  checked 5000 moves (and 4 targets h each): all OK
  delta(1) = delta(1/2) = 0 (both primary hostile points sit at the chart origin): True
  precision k(x) = v_3(x - h(x)) = 1 + v_3(delta(x)): OK
  kappa formula v_3(2^K - r) = [K=e mod 2](1 + v_3(K - kappa(r))), kappa(r) = log(r_1)/log(-2): 16000 cases, OK
  kappa(3m+1) = 2 i(m) (kappa IS the doubled trunk coordinate): OK

==============================================================================
P6  the functional-equation involution s -> 1-s in the trunk chart
==============================================================================
  M(m) = (1-m)/(3m+1).  Claim: T(1-s) = M(T(s)) for all s in Z_3.
  checked on 200 samples: OK
  M is an involution: M(M(m)) = m (exact, 20 rationals): True
  fixed points of M in Q: m = -1 (= T(1/2)) and m = 1/3 (not in Z_3); M(-1) = -1
  M(1) = 0, M(1/2) = 1/5, M(0) = 1, M(-1/2) = -3
  => the hostile set {1, 1/2} of the backward E-game is NOT M-invariant (1 -> 0 illegal, 1/2 -> 1/5
     generic): the E-game has no s <-> 1-s symmetry in the trunk chart.

