P9  |(s-1) zeta_3(s)|_3 = 3 at s = 1-k (von Staudt-Clausen), exact
==============================================================================
  even k <= 300: v_3((s-1) zeta_3(s)) = v_3((1-3^(k-1)) B_k) = -1 for all: True
  odd k <= 119:  v_3(k L(omega,1-k)) = v_3(B_(k,omega)) = -1 for all: True
  Proof (all k): for even k, (3-1) | k so 3 B_k = -1 mod 3; odd k similarly via B_(k,omega).
  Since the points 1-k are dense in Z_3 and (s-1)zeta_3(s) is continuous, |(s-1)zeta_3(s)|_3 = 3
  on all of Z_3: zeta_3 has NO zeros (in particular none at s = 1/2, none at s = i*).

