==============================================================================
P11 DRIFT/SHEET control: the trunk of every qx+1 map is an Iwasawa coordinate (q non-Wieferich)
==============================================================================
  trunk of qx+1 = {x : qx+1 is a power of 2} = {(u^i - 1)/q}, u = 2^ord_q(2).  LTE: v_q(u^i - 1) =
  v_q(u - 1) + v_q(i); so i -> (u^i-1)/q is an isometry of Z_q onto Z_q iff v_q(u - 1) = 1.
   q =     3: ord_q(2) =    2, u = 1+q (Mersenne prime)   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =     5: ord_q(2) =    4, u = 16                     v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =     7: ord_q(2) =    3, u = 1+q (Mersenne prime)   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =    11: ord_q(2) =   10, u = 1024                   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =    13: ord_q(2) =   12, u = 4096                   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =    17: ord_q(2) =    8, u = 256                    v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =    31: ord_q(2) =    5, u = 1+q (Mersenne prime)   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =   127: ord_q(2) =    7, u = 1+q (Mersenne prime)   v_q(u-1) = 1  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk IS an isometry onto Z_q
   q =  1093: ord_q(2) =  364, u = 2^364                  v_q(u-1) = 2  LTE check i<400: True  => trunk is NOT an isometry onto Z_q (Wieferich prime: image q^1Z_q)
  The 5x+1 and 7x+1 maps (expected to have divergent orbits) carry the same structure; 7x+1 even has
  u = 1+q exactly, like 3x+1.  The minus sheet uses the negated trunk.  So the identity is DRIFT- and
  SHEET-blind: it cannot carry information that distinguishes 3x+1 from its controls.

==============================================================================
P12 half-integer values: T(n/2) = ((-2)^n - 1)/3 and the exits of -1
==============================================================================
  T(n/2) = ((-2)^n - 1)/3 for -20 <= n <= 40 (since 4^(1/2) = -2 in 1+3Z_3): True
  hence T(n + 1/2) = -S(n) = -(2^(2n+1)+1)/3: the plus trunk passes through the negated minus trunk: True
  departure chart: delta(-1) = 1/2: True;  delta(-1/2) = -1/2: True;  delta(1) = delta(1/2) = 0
  plus-game reverse moves from -1 with k = 2n+1 land at -S(n) = T(n + 1/2): True
  So "s = 1/2" in the trunk chart is the first exit of the point -1 (a hostile point of the forward game
  and of the minus sheet), because log(-2)/log(4) = 1/2.  The number 1/2 here is the exponent relating the
  two generators -2 and 4 of 1+3Z_3.

