==============================================================================
D5  the E-game's own zeta: dynamical zeta of the canonical escape Psi
==============================================================================
   Psi has full branches (h,k), h in {1,1/2}, k >= 1, each a bijection of its shell onto Z_3^x,
   expanding by 3^k, with price rho_h(k); rho_(1/2)(k) = 2 rho_1(k) (the 1/2-thread pays one extra
   doubling).  For the weighted full shift the Ruelle zeta is 1/(1 - W), W(x;theta) =
   (1 + 2^theta) sum_k rho_1(k)^theta x^k, x = 3^-s  (rho_1(1)=1/3, rho_1(2)=4/9, rho_1(k) =
   2^floor(k log2 3)/3^k = 2^-{k log2 3} for k>=3).  Its poles are the "resonances".
   min_theta s(theta) = 0.64150 at theta* = 2.6735  (endgame note: dim_H Bad_Psi <= 0.64150)
   Lundberg exponent: W(1/3; theta_L) = 1 at theta_L = 8.6433  (endgame note: 8.6434)
   theta* (dimension): leading pole x_0 = 0.494228 (s = 0.64150); stable poles with |x| < 0.8 (3), as |x| and Re s = -log|x|/log 3:
      x = +0.494228+0.000000i   |x| = 0.494228   Re s = +0.64150   (Ihara-type critical value s_0/2 = 0.32075)
      x = -0.124207+0.762002i   |x| = 0.772059   Re s = +0.23547   (Ihara-type critical value s_0/2 = 0.32075)
      x = -0.124207-0.762002i   |x| = 0.772059   Re s = +0.23547   (Ihara-type critical value s_0/2 = 0.32075)
   theta_L (Lundberg): leading pole x_0 = 0.333333 (s = 1.00000); stable poles with |x| < 0.8 (7), as |x| and Re s = -log|x|/log 3:
      x = +0.333333+0.000000i   |x| = 0.333333   Re s = +1.00000   (Ihara-type critical value s_0/2 = 0.50000)
      x = -0.036860+0.367564i   |x| = 0.369408   Re s = +0.90647   (Ihara-type critical value s_0/2 = 0.50000)
